# R11: the six companion Connections, converted from the drafts in the vault's Companions/ files (Lane F), plus the seven that custom heroes meet.
# Each scene is started by a second entry of the villager in the location (a `when` on the companion in the party, their Incitement done and the Crooked House's
# witch dead: vessla_slain); it sets connection_<thread> and makes the villager Friendly. Closing the quest pays the Connection's Bless for a day and starts the Discovery's quest (story/fateweaving.gd).

~ thomasin_cordelia_start
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: Hold the lower left arm an inch higher so the brass tape clears the glass.
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: I know the pull of a tight seam along the ribs, and the thread has to give when you breathe.
thomasin_ardor [smile]: Try this charcoal silk on, I lined the ruby-glass buttonholes to cushion your vials.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You measured all eight shoulders without pausing once to ask what the surgeon left underneath.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My apologies, the collar sits to the millimetre, and I appear to have misplaced my phrasing.
* You two know what it takes to mend what others broke. -> thomasin_kin
* Ask her what holds up against alchemical heat. -> thomasin_fabric
* Thank the tailor and step out. -> thomasin_go

~ thomasin_kin
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: Glass leaves a jagged line when it goes in, and the needle leaves a straight one coming out.
thomasin_ardor [smile]: What matters is that the cloth lies flat over both.
interject name:cordelia_skein: A remarkably sound pathology, Miss Ardor, and I shall endeavour not to tear the gussets.
-> thomasin_close

~ thomasin_fabric
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: Double-weight charcoal silk under the arms, stitched with silver thread that will not char.
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: If a vial boils over, the lining takes the burn before your skin does.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Silver thread for thermal dissipation, darling, you put the academy quartermasters to shame.
-> thomasin_close

~ thomasin_go
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: The lamplight is always on if a button loosens in the wet.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Thank you, Miss Ardor, for the bias cut and the quiet.
-> thomasin_close

~ thomasin_close
thomasin_ardor [smile]: Wear it in good health, and let the lower cuffs hang loose when you climb.
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: Come back after the first rain so I can check how the silk settles.
set connection_evolution
quest connection_evolution met
quest discovery_evolution waiting
attitude thomasin_ardor friendly
set cordelia_waistcoat
-> END

~ alda_delphine_start
alda_farnum [smile]: Welcome to the Green Queen, my dears, though I see your table will require an extra place setting.
alda_farnum [sly]: Forgive the liberty, my dear, but a gentleman's invisible lapel should lie flat when he visits my house.
alda_farnum [smile]: Such lively company rarely lingers without a heavy ledger, so let me offer a house blessing for the story of how you met.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Keep your fingers off the billing, madam, Your Foolishness is very particular about his tailoring.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Though if your house blessing is half as warm as that spiced wine, we might discuss a matinee.
* Let her read the ledger. A free blessing's good business. -> alda_ledger
* Careful, she's pricing your stitches like cloth. -> alda_careful
* We want a room, not a reading. -> alda_room

~ alda_ledger
alda_farnum [smile]: Sensible friends are worth their weight in silver, and a good story pours better than vintage wine.
alda_farnum [sly]: We can tally the finer details by the hearth once your glasses are empty.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He says you are lying, and he doesn't even have eyes, so do keep your thumb off the scale.
-> alda_close

~ alda_careful
alda_farnum [smile]: I admire fine needlework wherever it walks in, and Picco felt is so rarely seen this far out.
alda_farnum [sly]: Every sturdy seam has its provenance, and I always pay fair market value for a rarity.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Touch a single thread on my cuff, darling, and we will see how neatly your own sleeves come unpicked.
-> alda_close

~ alda_room
alda_farnum [smile]: Of course, a clean key and a quiet door are the simplest transaction in the book.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Mind the stairs on the way up, darlings, our hostess counts the creaks on the floorboards.
-> alda_close

~ alda_close
alda_farnum [smile]: May the Green Queen keep your threads dry and your patron polite while you rest under my roof.
alda_farnum [sly]: When you are ready to settle the rest of the account, you know right where the counter is.
set connection_ascendancy
quest connection_ascendancy met
quest discovery_ascendancy waiting
attitude alda_farnum friendly
set delphine_tether_noted
-> END

~ hilda_lucan_start
hilda_brom [neutral]: Big wolf. Bigger dog. Both of you jumping at dry sky-rumble.
hilda_brom [smile]: Ha, look at you holding his ears like a mother hen in the pines.
hilda_brom [neutral]: Catch this pine-sprig. Smear the crow-grease on your cuffs. Look south-east to Foxwillow corn, where something worse than a fugitive stalks the rows.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, madam, I am merely shielding my hound's delicate auditory passages from an unscheduled meteorological report.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Though by the resin and carrion fat on these needles, your tracking preparation is a solid nine out of ten.
* You two hunt the same way. Hear her out. -> hilda_kin
* Careful, her spirit bear looks hungry. -> hilda_stare
* We have our trail. Thanks, Hilda. -> hilda_go

~ hilda_kin
hilda_brom [smile]: He talks like a book, your tall wolf. Nose works, though.
hilda_brom [neutral]: Keep the wind in your teeth when you hit the corn, Houndstooth.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: I shall endeavour to honour the Old Ways with proper posture, Madam Brom, if you please.
-> hilda_close

~ hilda_stare
hilda_brom [sly]: Bear only bites what runs. You do not look like a runner.
hilda_brom [neutral]: Keep your little ghost dog behind your boots in Foxwillow.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Dreadfang and I shall maintain a respectful distance from your magnificent ursine specimen, madam.
-> hilda_close

~ hilda_go
hilda_brom [neutral]: Good. Talk less, walk faster, corn is already moving.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Quite right, friends, let us take the south-east spoor before the scent thins.
-> hilda_close

~ hilda_close
hilda_brom [neutral]: May the Green Queen keep your throat whole and your claws sharp, book-wolf.
hilda_brom [smile]: Ha. Put a hat on that dog if it thunders again.
set connection_slaughter
quest connection_slaughter met
quest discovery_slaughter waiting
attitude hilda_brom friendly
set lucan_hilda_kin
-> END

~ mori_rook_start
mori_shade [neutral]: Warden, by the cut of the leather and the chalk under your nails. I have set out grey grave-wax and a stick of mason's chalk on the trestle.
mori_shade [neutral]: Your ledger is kept to a clean standard, Warden, dry edges and honest dates, the way Yorgrim kept Maidenmist Cemetery before he went quiet.
mori_shade [neutral]: I have marked one cross at the soured fields of Foxwillow, where the drainage fails and the dead lie uneasy. The other sites will show themselves to a working eye.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Proper tools, ma'am, and a clear map. Rare enough to find a parish office with the tallow dry and the records in order.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Hold on a second while I take a breath for the shift log. Keeps the ribs from sticking while we go over the zoning.
* You two talk like the same union. -> mori_union
* She's seen that badge, Rook. -> mori_badge
* Take the map and the chalk. Let's go. -> mori_go

~ mori_union
mori_shade [neutral]: There is only one trade when the candles burn down, stranger. We keep the boundary between those who walk and those who rest.
mori_shade [neutral]: A yard without a watchman is only a pantry for the dark.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Couldn't have phrased the bylaw cleaner myself, ma'am.
-> mori_close

~ mori_badge
mori_shade [neutral]: I do not look at brass, nor ask what snow it came through. Brass is only brass.
mori_shade [neutral]: What counts in this valley is the hand that holds the shovel, and what the pin is fastened to.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Noted and appreciated, ma'am.
-> mori_close

~ mori_go
mori_shade [neutral]: Walk with a measured step on the Foxwillow clay, for the turf is thin over the old pits.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Chalk's pocketed, wax is stowed, docket's open.
-> mori_close

~ mori_close
mori_shade [neutral]: May the earth lie level under your boots, Warden, and may your own bones keep the cold that steadies them.
mori_shade [neutral]: Come back to this room when you have a fresh page filled.
set connection_pilgrimage
quest connection_pilgrimage met
quest discovery_pilgrimage waiting
attitude mori_shade friendly
set rook_mori_met
-> END

~ holly_silas_start
holly_aster [smile]: Take this loaf while the crust is still singing, before Violet and Lavender turn my cooling racks into a fort.
holly_aster [smile]: Don't mind your little shadow tapping at my wrist, it's only a grey spade-mark I've carried since the cradle.
holly_aster [smile]: An unseen creditor holds the deed to my thirty-fifth birthday, and the only ledger office floats on that neon riverboat at the Drowned Crossroads.
interject name:silas_vane: One taste on the draught says toasted caraway, woodsmoke, and a very familiar landlord writing in the margins, friend.
interject name:silas_vane: My shadow only taps a mark when it recognizes the house ink on the skin.
* We'll tear your page out too. -> holly_oath
* What did the creditor take for it? -> holly_price
* Take the loaf. Leave her in peace. -> holly_loaf

~ holly_oath
holly_aster [afraid]: Keep your voice down over the oven's roar, or my girls will think we're telling ghost stories before supper.
holly_aster [afraid]: If you're truly boarding that riverboat, don't let him deal you from the bottom of the shoe.
interject name:silas_vane: House always wins, unless you burn the house, and I brought plenty of dry kindling, friend.
-> holly_close

~ holly_price
holly_aster [sad]: Every woman in my line gets thirty-five bright years to bake the bread and raise the girls, and then the tab comes due.
holly_aster [sad]: My mother paid it, her mother paid it, and my birthday falls in just a few weeks.
interject name:silas_vane: Sounds like a rigged game passed down the table, and I never could stand a crooked shoe.
-> holly_close

~ holly_loaf
holly_aster [smile]: That's sensible talk, because a warm rye loaf is a much safer thing to carry than a baker's bad luck.
interject name:silas_vane: Never walked away from a marked table yet, friend, even when I'm just buying the bread.
-> holly_close

~ holly_close
holly_aster [smile]: Hold out your palm and take this pinch of blessed hearth-salt, the Old Ways say it keeps a creditor's ink from drying.
holly_aster [smile]: Now eat that crust before it cools, or I'll charge you double just for standing in my flour.
set connection_liberation
quest connection_liberation met
quest discovery_liberation waiting
attitude holly_aster friendly
set liberation_holly_page_seen
-> END

~ rain_tobin_start
sister_rain [smile]: That is a surgeon's knot on a pumpkin stem, friend, and the sap is already settling.
sister_rain [sad]: Oh, your poor collarbone is as dry and aching as the soil under this green.
sister_rain [neutral]: The Patient Lady says we tend what grows and bind what splits, and we never answer blight with a torch.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Careful on the collarbone, miss, it's old wood and dry.
interject name:tobin_hayward: A clean splice stops the bleeding, that is just sound husbandry, no sermon required.
* Her way makes sense. You can't heal soil by scorching it. -> rain_gentle
* Patience is fine for daisies, not for a plague. -> rain_blunt
* Take her blessing. We should keep moving. -> rain_go

~ rain_gentle
sister_rain [smile]: You hear that, mister scarecrow, your friends have the right of it.
sister_rain [neutral]: Ash never grew an apple yet, no matter how deep the rot went.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good soil, bad seed, and a great deal of weeding left to do before anyone talks of apples.
-> rain_close

~ rain_blunt
sister_rain [angry]: Bite your tongue, the land is bleeding enough without you calling down iron and fire on it!
sister_rain [smile]: Listen to me roaring like a March gale when your friend here just saved my best pumpkin.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You have a brisk way with a congregation, I will give you that much.
-> rain_close

~ rain_go
sister_rain [smile]: Always rushing off, you travellers, though at least this one stops to mend a vine.
interject name:tobin_hayward: A split stem is a split stem, and it takes ten seconds to tie it right.
-> rain_close

~ rain_close
sister_rain [smile]: Walk in the Lady's patience, stitched man, and don't pluck what grows from your cuff.
sister_rain [sad]: When you have the stomach for worse than a bruised vine, the sick places round the village are crying out for a steady hand.
set connection_rejuvenation
quest connection_rejuvenation met
quest discovery_rejuvenation waiting
attitude sister_rain friendly
-> END
